            "body": "Ab tak aapne do equations ko hal karne ke chaar tareeke seekhe: substitution, elimination, cross-multiplication aur graph. Topic 4 mein Vihaan aur Zara ki sadkein chowk (3, 2) par kaati thi, aur graph se ye bhi dekha ki do linear equations ke 0, 1 ya anginat solutions ho sakte hain. In sab mein ek baat common thi: equations **x aur y ki seedhi line wali** (linear) thi, jaise 2x + 3y = 13.\n\nAaj ek naya sawaal: agar equation dekhne mein linear **na** lage, to kya hum apne purane tareeke chhod dein? Bilkul nahi. Aaj seekhenge ki kuch \"badmaash\" equations apna **bhes badal kar** aati hain, aur ek chhota sa naam badalte hi unka asli, linear chehra saamne aa jata hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak aapne do equations ko hal karne ke chaar tareeke seekhe: substitution, elimination, cross-multiplication aur graph. Topic 4 mein Vihaan aur Zara ki sadkein chowk (3, 2) par kaati thi, aur graph se ye bhi dekha ki do linear equations ke 0, 1 ya anginat solutions ho sakte hain. In sab mein ek baat common thi: equations **x aur y ki seedhi line wali** (linear) thi, jaise 2x + 3y = 13.\n\nAaj ek naya sawaal: agar equation dekhne mein linear **na** lage, to kya hum apne purane tareeke chhod dein? Bilkul nahi. Aaj seekhenge ki kuch \"badmaash\" equations apna **bhes badal kar** aati hain, aur ek chhota sa naam badalte hi unka asli, linear chehra saamne aa jata hai."
