          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. The sum of two numbers is 41 and their difference is 9. Find the numbers.\n\n2. One number is 5 less than three times another number. The sum of the two numbers is 63. Find the numbers.\n\n3. A mother is 3 times as old as her daughter. After 12 years, the mother will be twice as old as her daughter. Find their present ages.\n\n4. 4 years ago, an uncle was 5 times as old as his nephew. 4 years from now, the uncle will be 3 times as old as the nephew. Find their present ages.\n\n5. A fraction becomes 9/11 when 2 is added to both its numerator and denominator, and becomes 5/6 when 3 is added to both. Find the fraction.\n\n6. The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 11. If the digits are reversed, the new number is 27 more than the original. Find the original number.\n\n7. A two-digit number is 4 times the sum of its digits. If the digits are reversed, the new number is 18 more than the original. Find the number.\n\n8. (a) A student writes a two-digit number with tens digit x and units digit y as \"xy\". Explain what is wrong and write the correct expression.\n   (b) The sum of the present ages of two friends is 30 and one is 40 years older than the other. Set up the equations, solve them, and say why the answer shows that the problem cannot be right.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. Bada = x, chhota = y. x + y = 41 aur x − y = 9. Jodne par 2x = 50, x = 25, y = 16.\n   Jaanch: 25 + 16 = 41 ✅, 25 − 16 = 9 ✅. Numbers **25 aur 16**.\n\n2. Doosra number = y, pehla = x. x = 3y − 5 aur x + y = 63. Daalo: 3y − 5 + y = 63, 4y = 68, y = 17, x = 3(17) − 5 = 46.\n   Jaanch: 3 × 17 = 51, 51 − 5 = 46 ✅. 46 + 17 = 63 ✅. Numbers **46 aur 17**.\n\n3. Maa x, beti y. x = 3y. 12 saal baad x + 12 = 2(y + 12). Daalo: 3y + 12 = 2y + 24, y = 12, x = 36.\n   Jaanch: 36 = 3 × 12 ✅. 12 saal baad 48 aur 24, 48 = 2 × 24 ✅. Maa **36 saal** ki, beti **12 saal** ki.\n\n4. Uncle x, nephew y. 4 saal pehle: x − 4 = 5(y − 4), to x = 5y − 16. 4 saal baad: x + 4 = 3(y + 4), to x = 3y + 8. Barabar karo: 5y − 16 = 3y + 8, 2y = 24, y = 12, x = 3(12) + 8 = 44.\n   Jaanch: 4 saal pehle 40 aur 8, 40 = 5 × 8 ✅. 4 saal baad 48 aur 16, 48 = 3 × 16 ✅. Uncle **44 saal** ke, nephew **12 saal** ka.\n\n5. Fraction x/y. (x + 2)/(y + 2) = 9/11: 11x + 22 = 9y + 18, to 11x − 9y = −4 ... (1). (x + 3)/(y + 3) = 5/6: 6x + 18 = 5y + 15, to 6x − 5y = −3 ... (2).\n   (1) ko 5 se aur (2) ko 9 se guna karo: 55x − 45y = −20 aur 54x − 45y = −27. Ghatane par x = 7. (2) se 42 − 5y = −3, 5y = 45, y = 9.\n   Jaanch: (7 + 2)/(9 + 2) = 9/11 ✅. (7 + 3)/(9 + 3) = 10/12 = 5/6 ✅. Fraction **7/9**.\n\n6. Tens x, units y. x + y = 11. Reverse 27 zyada: 9(y − x) = 27, to y − x = 3. Jodne par 2y = 14, y = 7, x = 4.\n   Jaanch: number 47. Digit sum 4 + 7 = 11 ✅. Reverse 74, 74 − 47 = 27 ✅. Number **47**.\n\n7. Tens x, units y. 10x + y = 4(x + y), to 6x = 3y, y = 2x. Reverse 18 zyada: 9(y − x) = 18, y − x = 2. Daalo: 2x − x = 2, x = 2, y = 4.\n   Jaanch: number 24. Digit sum 6, 4 × 6 = 24 ✅. Reverse 42, 42 − 24 = 18 ✅. Number **24**.\n\n8. (a) \"xy\" ka algebra mein matlab x × y hota hai, number nahi. Jaise x = 3, y = 6 ho, to xy = 18, par number 36 hai. Sahi: **10x + y**.\n   (b) Friends x aur y, x bada. x + y = 30 aur x − y = 40. Jodne par 2x = 70, x = 35, y = −5. Umar negative nahi ho sakti, isliye ye sawaal mumkin nahi hai. Jaanch: x − y = 35 − (−5) = 40 aur x + y = 35 + (−5) = 30 to milte hain, par umar −5 ho hi nahi sakti. Asal baat: jab sum 30 ho, to antar 30 se zyada ho hi nahi sakta.\n\nAaj aapne wo seekha jo sabse kaam ki cheez hai: kisi bhi sawaal ko shabdon se equation mein badalna. Jab bhi atko, pehle x aur y ka matlab likho, aur aakhir mein jawab ko sawaal ke vaakyon mein daalkar dekho.\n\n**Aage kya?** Abhi tak numbers, umar, fractions aur digits ki baat hui. Topic 7 mein hum aur aage badhenge: paise aur keemat ke sawaal, gaadi ki speed aur doori, nadi mein naav, aur geometry ki chhoti-chhoti paheliyan. Wahan bhi wahi chaar kadam kaam aayenge.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. The sum of two numbers is 41 and their difference is 9. Find the numbers.\n\n2. One number is 5 less than three times another number. The sum of the two numbers is 63. Find the numbers.\n\n3. A mother is 3 times as old as her daughter. After 12 years, the mother will be twice as old as her daughter. Find their present ages.\n\n4. 4 years ago, an uncle was 5 times as old as his nephew. 4 years from now, the uncle will be 3 times as old as the nephew. Find their present ages.\n\n5. A fraction becomes 9/11 when 2 is added to both its numerator and denominator, and becomes 5/6 when 3 is added to both. Find the fraction.\n\n6. The sum of the digits of a two-digit number is 11. If the digits are reversed, the new number is 27 more than the original. Find the original number.\n\n7. A two-digit number is 4 times the sum of its digits. If the digits are reversed, the new number is 18 more than the original. Find the number.\n\n8. (a) A student writes a two-digit number with tens digit x and units digit y as \"xy\". Explain what is wrong and write the correct expression.\n   (b) The sum of the present ages of two friends is 30 and one is 40 years older than the other. Set up the equations, solve them, and say why the answer shows that the problem cannot be right.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. Bada = x, chhota = y. x + y = 41 aur x − y = 9. Jodne par 2x = 50, x = 25, y = 16.\n   Jaanch: 25 + 16 = 41 ✅, 25 − 16 = 9 ✅. Numbers **25 aur 16**.\n\n2. Doosra number = y, pehla = x. x = 3y − 5 aur x + y = 63. Daalo: 3y − 5 + y = 63, 4y = 68, y = 17, x = 3(17) − 5 = 46.\n   Jaanch: 3 × 17 = 51, 51 − 5 = 46 ✅. 46 + 17 = 63 ✅. Numbers **46 aur 17**.\n\n3. Maa x, beti y. x = 3y. 12 saal baad x + 12 = 2(y + 12). Daalo: 3y + 12 = 2y + 24, y = 12, x = 36.\n   Jaanch: 36 = 3 × 12 ✅. 12 saal baad 48 aur 24, 48 = 2 × 24 ✅. Maa **36 saal** ki, beti **12 saal** ki.\n\n4. Uncle x, nephew y. 4 saal pehle: x − 4 = 5(y − 4), to x = 5y − 16. 4 saal baad: x + 4 = 3(y + 4), to x = 3y + 8. Barabar karo: 5y − 16 = 3y + 8, 2y = 24, y = 12, x = 3(12) + 8 = 44.\n   Jaanch: 4 saal pehle 40 aur 8, 40 = 5 × 8 ✅. 4 saal baad 48 aur 16, 48 = 3 × 16 ✅. Uncle **44 saal** ke, nephew **12 saal** ka.\n\n5. Fraction x/y. (x + 2)/(y + 2) = 9/11: 11x + 22 = 9y + 18, to 11x − 9y = −4 ... (1). (x + 3)/(y + 3) = 5/6: 6x + 18 = 5y + 15, to 6x − 5y = −3 ... (2).\n   (1) ko 5 se aur (2) ko 9 se guna karo: 55x − 45y = −20 aur 54x − 45y = −27. Ghatane par x = 7. (2) se 42 − 5y = −3, 5y = 45, y = 9.\n   Jaanch: (7 + 2)/(9 + 2) = 9/11 ✅. (7 + 3)/(9 + 3) = 10/12 = 5/6 ✅. Fraction **7/9**.\n\n6. Tens x, units y. x + y = 11. Reverse 27 zyada: 9(y − x) = 27, to y − x = 3. Jodne par 2y = 14, y = 7, x = 4.\n   Jaanch: number 47. Digit sum 4 + 7 = 11 ✅. Reverse 74, 74 − 47 = 27 ✅. Number **47**.\n\n7. Tens x, units y. 10x + y = 4(x + y), to 6x = 3y, y = 2x. Reverse 18 zyada: 9(y − x) = 18, y − x = 2. Daalo: 2x − x = 2, x = 2, y = 4.\n   Jaanch: number 24. Digit sum 6, 4 × 6 = 24 ✅. Reverse 42, 42 − 24 = 18 ✅. Number **24**.\n\n8. (a) \"xy\" ka algebra mein matlab x × y hota hai, number nahi. Jaise x = 3, y = 6 ho, to xy = 18, par number 36 hai. Sahi: **10x + y**.\n   (b) Friends x aur y, x bada. x + y = 30 aur x − y = 40. Jodne par 2x = 70, x = 35, y = −5. Umar negative nahi ho sakti, isliye ye sawaal mumkin nahi hai. Jaanch: x − y = 35 − (−5) = 40 aur x + y = 35 + (−5) = 30 to milte hain, par umar −5 ho hi nahi sakti. Asal baat: jab sum 30 ho, to antar 30 se zyada ho hi nahi sakta.\n\nAaj aapne wo seekha jo sabse kaam ki cheez hai: kisi bhi sawaal ko shabdon se equation mein badalna. Jab bhi atko, pehle x aur y ka matlab likho, aur aakhir mein jawab ko sawaal ke vaakyon mein daalkar dekho.\n\n**Aage kya?** Abhi tak numbers, umar, fractions aur digits ki baat hui. Topic 7 mein hum aur aage badhenge: paise aur keemat ke sawaal, gaadi ki speed aur doori, nadi mein naav, aur geometry ki chhoti-chhoti paheliyan. Wahan bhi wahi chaar kadam kaam aayenge."
          }
