            "body": "Scout camp mein Mr. Pillai ne do ped ke beech ek lambi rassi kas ke bandh di. Ped ke paas rassi ke sire par do khoonte hain: bayein khoonte ko naam do **A**, dayein ko **B**. Rassi seedhi tani hui hai, A se B tak.\n\nMr. Pillai ne scout Omkar se kaha, \"Raat ko is rassi ke **bilkul beech mein** lantern latkana hai. Par measuring tape nahi hai. Mere paas bas ye string ka loop aur ek stick hai. Bata, kaise karega?\"\n\nOmkar ne socha: \"Aankh se andaaza lagaun? Agar thoda bhi idhar-udhar hua, to lantern ek taraf jhuka rahega.\" Phir usne ek chaal soochi. String ke ek sire ko khoonte A par pakda, doosre sire par stick bandhi, string ko kas kar tana, aur stick se zameen par **ek gol arc** kheench diya. Phir wahi string, bina chhoti-badi kiye, khoonte B par pakadi, aur B se bhi arc kheencha. Dono arcs rassi ke upar aur neeche ek-ek jagah mile. Un dono milne wali jagahon ko jodne wali seedhi line ne rassi ko jahan kaata, wahi tha rassi ka **ekdum beech**.\n\nMr. Pillai ne rassi ko modkar dekha, A wala sira B wale sire par rakha, to modi hui jagah wahi thi. Omkar ne usi jagah lantern tang diya.\n\nKya Omkar ne jaadu kiya? Nahi. Usne ek hi tareeka use kiya, jise geometry mein **perpendicular bisector** kehte hain. Is topic ke end mein hum is rassi wali figure ko poori tarah banayenge, kadam-dar-kadam. Pehle apni geometry box se mil lete hain.",
