          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "### 1. Minus galat order mein\n\nLeg nikalte waqt **bade square mein se chhota** minus karo.\n- Galat: Hypotenuse 13, leg 5: 5² − 13² = 25 − 169 = −144. Negative square aa gaya, ye ho hi nahi sakta.\n- Sahi: 13² − 5² = 169 − 25 = 144, to leg = **12**\n\n### 2. Square root lena bhool jana\n\n- Galat: Legs 6 aur 8: c² = 36 + 64 = 100, \"to c = 100\".\n- Sahi: c² = 100 to c = √100 = **10**\n\nJaanch tarika: 100 metre ki seedhi to bahut hi lambi hoti, jabki legs sirf 6 aur 8 the. Hypotenuse legs se lambi hoti hai, par itni nahi.\n\n### 3. Surd ko simplify na karna\n\n- Galat: c = √72 ko wahi chhod dena.\n- Sahi: √72 = √36 × √2 = **6√2** ≈ 6 × 1.414 = **8.49**\n\nJawab sahi hota hai, par simplify karna zaroori hai taaki jawab saaf dikhe.\n\n### 4. Galat side ko hypotenuse maan lena\n\nTriangle ke sides 7, 24 aur 25 hain, aur 7 aur 25 diye hain, 24 poochna hai.\n- Galat: 7² + 25² = 49 + 625 = 674. (25 hypotenuse hai, use jodna nahi tha!)\n- Sahi: Hypotenuse sabse lambi side hai, right angle ke saamne: **25**. To 24² = 25² − 7² = 625 − 49 = 576, **24**\n\n### 5. Har triangle par formula laga dena\n\nc² = a² + b² sirf **right triangle** ke liye hai. Agar sawaal mein right angle ki baat hi nahi hai, to ye mat lagao. (Ye ulti baat, yaani \"agar sides aisi hon to kya triangle right hota hai?\", aage dekhenge.)",
            "bodyHinglish": "### 1. Minus galat order mein\n\nLeg nikalte waqt **bade square mein se chhota** minus karo.\n- Galat: Hypotenuse 13, leg 5: 5² − 13² = 25 − 169 = −144. Negative square aa gaya, ye ho hi nahi sakta.\n- Sahi: 13² − 5² = 169 − 25 = 144, to leg = **12**\n\n### 2. Square root lena bhool jana\n\n- Galat: Legs 6 aur 8: c² = 36 + 64 = 100, \"to c = 100\".\n- Sahi: c² = 100 to c = √100 = **10**\n\nJaanch tarika: 100 metre ki seedhi to bahut hi lambi hoti, jabki legs sirf 6 aur 8 the. Hypotenuse legs se lambi hoti hai, par itni nahi.\n\n### 3. Surd ko simplify na karna\n\n- Galat: c = √72 ko wahi chhod dena.\n- Sahi: √72 = √36 × √2 = **6√2** ≈ 6 × 1.414 = **8.49**\n\nJawab sahi hota hai, par simplify karna zaroori hai taaki jawab saaf dikhe.\n\n### 4. Galat side ko hypotenuse maan lena\n\nTriangle ke sides 7, 24 aur 25 hain, aur 7 aur 25 diye hain, 24 poochna hai.\n- Galat: 7² + 25² = 49 + 625 = 674. (25 hypotenuse hai, use jodna nahi tha!)\n- Sahi: Hypotenuse sabse lambi side hai, right angle ke saamne: **25**. To 24² = 25² − 7² = 625 − 49 = 576, **24**\n\n### 5. Har triangle par formula laga dena\n\nc² = a² + b² sirf **right triangle** ke liye hai. Agar sawaal mein right angle ki baat hi nahi hai, to ye mat lagao. (Ye ulti baat, yaani \"agar sides aisi hon to kya triangle right hota hai?\", aage dekhenge.)"
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- Hypotenuse: **c = √(a² + b²)** (squares **jodo**, phir root lo).\n- Leg: **a = √(c² − b²)** (hypotenuse ke square mein se **minus**, phir root).\n- Jawab surd ho sakta hai: √50 = 5√2, √32 = 4√2. Simplify karo.\n- Pythagorean triplets: 3-4-5, 5-12-13, 8-15-17, 7-24-25, 20-21-29. Inke multiples bhi triplets hain.\n- m > 1 ke liye (2m, m² − 1, m² + 1) triplet deta hai (m = 2, 3, 4: 4-3-5, 6-8-10, 8-15-17).\n- Seedhi, screen, rectangle ka diagonal, raasta, wire, equilateral triangle ki height (√3/2)a, rhombus: sab right triangles hain.\n- Hypotenuse hamesha right angle ke saamne aur sabse lambi side hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "- Hypotenuse: **c = √(a² + b²)** (squares **jodo**, phir root lo).\n- Leg: **a = √(c² − b²)** (hypotenuse ke square mein se **minus**, phir root).\n- Jawab surd ho sakta hai: √50 = 5√2, √32 = 4√2. Simplify karo.\n- Pythagorean triplets: 3-4-5, 5-12-13, 8-15-17, 7-24-25, 20-21-29. Inke multiples bhi triplets hain.\n- m > 1 ke liye (2m, m² − 1, m² + 1) triplet deta hai (m = 2, 3, 4: 4-3-5, 6-8-10, 8-15-17).\n- Seedhi, screen, rectangle ka diagonal, raasta, wire, equilateral triangle ki height (√3/2)a, rhombus: sab right triangles hain.\n- Hypotenuse hamesha right angle ke saamne aur sabse lambi side hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. The two legs of a right triangle are 24 cm and 7 cm. Find the hypotenuse.\n2. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is 29 cm and one leg is 20 cm. Find the other leg.\n3. Find the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs 4 cm and 6 cm. Give the answer as a simplified surd.\n4. A right triangle has hypotenuse 12 cm and one leg 8 cm. Find the other leg as a simplified surd.\n5. A 17 m ladder reaches a window that is 15 m above the ground. How far is the foot of the ladder from the wall?\n6. The foot of a 10 m ladder is 6 m from a wall. The foot is pulled 2 m further away from the wall. How far does the top of the ladder slide down?\n7. The diagonal of a rectangle is 25 cm and one side is 7 cm. Find the other side and the perimeter.\n8. The diagonals of a rhombus are 10 cm and 24 cm. Find its side and perimeter.\n9. Find the height of an equilateral triangle of side 14 cm. Give the answer in surd form and approximately.\n10. Use the formula (2m, m² − 1, m² + 1) with m = 7 to make a triplet, and check it.\n11. Which of these are Pythagorean triplets? (a) 33, 56, 65 (b) 6, 9, 11 (c) 12, 16, 20 (d) 9, 12, 16\n12. A girl walks 15 m south and then 8 m east. What is the shortest distance back to her starting point?\n13. True or false? (a) c² = a² + b² works for every triangle. (b) Doubling a Pythagorean triplet gives another triplet. (c) The hypotenuse is always the longest side of a right triangle. (d) √(a² + b²) = a + b.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. c² = 24² + 7² = 576 + 49 = 625, c = **25 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 7² + 24² = 625 = 25² ✅\n\n2. b² = 29² − 20² = 841 − 400 = 441, b = **21 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 20² + 21² = 400 + 441 = 841 ✅\n\n3. c² = 16 + 36 = 52, c = √52 = √4 × √13 = **2√13 cm** ≈ 7.21 cm.\n   Jaanch: (2√13)² = 4 × 13 = 52 ✅\n\n4. b² = 144 − 64 = 80, b = √80 = √16 × √5 = **4√5 cm** ≈ 8.94 cm.\n   Jaanch: 80 + 64 = 144 ✅\n\n5. x² = 17² − 15² = 289 − 225 = 64, x = **8 m**.\n   Jaanch: 8² + 15² = 64 + 225 = 289 ✅\n\n6. Pehle ooncha = √(10² − 6²) = √64 = 8 m. Paer 6 + 2 = 8 m door hone par ooncha = √(10² − 8²) = √36 = 6 m. Top **2 m** neeche sarka.\n   Jaanch: 8² + 6² = 100 ✅\n\n7. Doosri side² = 625 − 49 = 576, side = **24 cm**. Perimeter = 2(24 + 7) = **62 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 7² + 24² = 625 ✅\n\n8. Aadhe diagonals 5 aur 12. Side² = 25 + 144 = 169, side = **13 cm**. Perimeter = 4 × 13 = **52 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 5² + 12² = 13² ✅\n\n9. h = (√3/2) × 14 = **7√3 cm** ≈ 7 × 1.732 = **12.12 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 14² − 7² = 196 − 49 = 147 = 49 × 3, √147 = 7√3 ✅\n\n10. m = 7: 2m = 14, m² − 1 = 48, m² + 1 = 50. Triplet **(14, 48, 50)**.\n    Jaanch: 14² + 48² = 196 + 2304 = 2500 = 50² ✅ (ye 7-24-25 ka double hai.)\n\n11. (a) 1089 + 3136 = 4225 = 65², **haan** ✅. (b) 36 + 81 = 117, par 11² = 121, **nahi** ❌. (c) 144 + 256 = 400 = 20², **haan** ✅ (4 × 3-4-5). (d) 81 + 144 = 225, par 16² = 256, **nahi** ❌ (sabse lambi side 16 hai, 225 ka root 15 hota).\n\n12. d² = 15² + 8² = 225 + 64 = 289, d = **17 m**.\n    Jaanch: 8-15-17 triplet ✅\n\n13. (a) **False** ❌. Sirf right triangle ke liye.\n    (b) **True** ✅. k² wali baat se.\n    (c) **True** ✅. Hypotenuse sabse lambi hoti hai.\n    (d) **False** ❌. Jaise a = 3, b = 4: √25 = 5, par 3 + 4 = 7.\n\nParul ab fire drill ki har seedhi ko ek right triangle ki tarah dekhti hai. Aap bhi jab agli baar kisi deewar se lagi seedhi ya kisi screen ko dekho, to uske andar chhupa triangle dhoondho.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab tak humne maana ki triangle right-angled hai aur side nikaali. Par ek ulta sawaal bhi hai: agar kisi triangle ki **teeno sides pata hon** aur right angle ka koi nishaan na ho, to kya sirf sides dekh kar bata sakte hain ki wo right triangle hai ya nahi? Topic 3 mein is ulte sawaal ka jawab milega.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. The two legs of a right triangle are 24 cm and 7 cm. Find the hypotenuse.\n2. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is 29 cm and one leg is 20 cm. Find the other leg.\n3. Find the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs 4 cm and 6 cm. Give the answer as a simplified surd.\n4. A right triangle has hypotenuse 12 cm and one leg 8 cm. Find the other leg as a simplified surd.\n5. A 17 m ladder reaches a window that is 15 m above the ground. How far is the foot of the ladder from the wall?\n6. The foot of a 10 m ladder is 6 m from a wall. The foot is pulled 2 m further away from the wall. How far does the top of the ladder slide down?\n7. The diagonal of a rectangle is 25 cm and one side is 7 cm. Find the other side and the perimeter.\n8. The diagonals of a rhombus are 10 cm and 24 cm. Find its side and perimeter.\n9. Find the height of an equilateral triangle of side 14 cm. Give the answer in surd form and approximately.\n10. Use the formula (2m, m² − 1, m² + 1) with m = 7 to make a triplet, and check it.\n11. Which of these are Pythagorean triplets? (a) 33, 56, 65 (b) 6, 9, 11 (c) 12, 16, 20 (d) 9, 12, 16\n12. A girl walks 15 m south and then 8 m east. What is the shortest distance back to her starting point?\n13. True or false? (a) c² = a² + b² works for every triangle. (b) Doubling a Pythagorean triplet gives another triplet. (c) The hypotenuse is always the longest side of a right triangle. (d) √(a² + b²) = a + b.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. c² = 24² + 7² = 576 + 49 = 625, c = **25 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 7² + 24² = 625 = 25² ✅\n\n2. b² = 29² − 20² = 841 − 400 = 441, b = **21 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 20² + 21² = 400 + 441 = 841 ✅\n\n3. c² = 16 + 36 = 52, c = √52 = √4 × √13 = **2√13 cm** ≈ 7.21 cm.\n   Jaanch: (2√13)² = 4 × 13 = 52 ✅\n\n4. b² = 144 − 64 = 80, b = √80 = √16 × √5 = **4√5 cm** ≈ 8.94 cm.\n   Jaanch: 80 + 64 = 144 ✅\n\n5. x² = 17² − 15² = 289 − 225 = 64, x = **8 m**.\n   Jaanch: 8² + 15² = 64 + 225 = 289 ✅\n\n6. Pehle ooncha = √(10² − 6²) = √64 = 8 m. Paer 6 + 2 = 8 m door hone par ooncha = √(10² − 8²) = √36 = 6 m. Top **2 m** neeche sarka.\n   Jaanch: 8² + 6² = 100 ✅\n\n7. Doosri side² = 625 − 49 = 576, side = **24 cm**. Perimeter = 2(24 + 7) = **62 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 7² + 24² = 625 ✅\n\n8. Aadhe diagonals 5 aur 12. Side² = 25 + 144 = 169, side = **13 cm**. Perimeter = 4 × 13 = **52 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 5² + 12² = 13² ✅\n\n9. h = (√3/2) × 14 = **7√3 cm** ≈ 7 × 1.732 = **12.12 cm**.\n   Jaanch: 14² − 7² = 196 − 49 = 147 = 49 × 3, √147 = 7√3 ✅\n\n10. m = 7: 2m = 14, m² − 1 = 48, m² + 1 = 50. Triplet **(14, 48, 50)**.\n    Jaanch: 14² + 48² = 196 + 2304 = 2500 = 50² ✅ (ye 7-24-25 ka double hai.)\n\n11. (a) 1089 + 3136 = 4225 = 65², **haan** ✅. (b) 36 + 81 = 117, par 11² = 121, **nahi** ❌. (c) 144 + 256 = 400 = 20², **haan** ✅ (4 × 3-4-5). (d) 81 + 144 = 225, par 16² = 256, **nahi** ❌ (sabse lambi side 16 hai, 225 ka root 15 hota).\n\n12. d² = 15² + 8² = 225 + 64 = 289, d = **17 m**.\n    Jaanch: 8-15-17 triplet ✅\n\n13. (a) **False** ❌. Sirf right triangle ke liye.\n    (b) **True** ✅. k² wali baat se.\n    (c) **True** ✅. Hypotenuse sabse lambi hoti hai.\n    (d) **False** ❌. Jaise a = 3, b = 4: √25 = 5, par 3 + 4 = 7.\n\nParul ab fire drill ki har seedhi ko ek right triangle ki tarah dekhti hai. Aap bhi jab agli baar kisi deewar se lagi seedhi ya kisi screen ko dekho, to uske andar chhupa triangle dhoondho.\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab tak humne maana ki triangle right-angled hai aur side nikaali. Par ek ulta sawaal bhi hai: agar kisi triangle ki **teeno sides pata hon** aur right angle ka koi nishaan na ho, to kya sirf sides dekh kar bata sakte hain ki wo right triangle hai ya nahi? Topic 3 mein is ulte sawaal ka jawab milega."
          }
