            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Ab tak hamara rasta ek hi disha mein tha: triangle right-angled ho, to uski sides ka rishta a² + b² = c² hota hai. Topic 1 mein Aditi ne (a + b)² wale bade square se iska proof dikhaya (aur similar triangles wale proof ki jhalak), aur Topic 2 mein Parul ne Balwant ji ki 10 m seedhi ka paer deewar se 6 m door nikala, saath mein missing side, triplets (3-4-5, 5-12-13, 8-15-17...) aur rectangle ke diagonal jaise kaam seekhe. Har jagah pehle se pata tha ki **90° ka angle maujood hai**.\n\nAb ek ulta sawaal: agar kisi triangle ke bas **teeno sides di hon** aur angle ka kuch pata na ho, to kya sides ke square dekhkar hi bata sakte hain ki 90° wala angle hai ya nahi? Jawab haan hai, aur ye is topic ka main idea hai. Chapter ka aakhri topic hai, to end mein poore chapter ka wrap-up aur triplets ki cheat-sheet bhi hogi.",
