          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: Radius aur diameter mein confusion**\nDiameter = 2 × radius. Agar question mein diameter diya hai aur formula mein r chahiye, to pehle aadha karo. Diameter 14 hai to r = 7, 14 nahi.\n\n**Galti 2: Position check karte waqt diameter se compare karna**\nDoori hamesha **radius** se compare hoti hai. Diameter 12, doori 7: r = 6, to point **bahar** hai, andar nahi.\n\n**Galti 3: Har chord ko diameter samajhna**\nSirf wahi chord diameter hai jo **centre se guzre**. Har diameter chord hai, par har chord diameter nahi.\n\n**Galti 4: Circle aur circular region ko ek samajhna**\nCircle sirf **kinaara (boundary)** hai. Kinaara + andar ka hissa = circular region. Chudi ek circle jaisi hai, roti ek circular region jaisi.\n\n**Galti 5: Circle aur circumference ko ek samajhna**\nCircle ek **shape** hai. Circumference us shape ki **lambai** (ek number) hai.\n\n**Galti 6: Tangent ko do points par kaatne wali line samajhna**\nDo points par kaatne wali line **secant** hai. Tangent sirf **ek point** par chhooti hai.\n\n**Galti 7: Centre ko circle par maan lena**\nCentre circle ke **andar** hota hai. Circle ke saare points centre se r doori par hain, aur centre ki apni doori 0 hai.\n\n**Galti 8: Arc aur chord ko ek samajhna**\nChord **seedha** line segment hai. Arc circle ka **curve wala** tukda hai. Chudi ka toota tukda arc hai, uske dono siron ko jodne wala seedha dhaaga chord hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: Radius aur diameter mein confusion**\nDiameter = 2 × radius. Agar question mein diameter diya hai aur formula mein r chahiye, to pehle aadha karo. Diameter 14 hai to r = 7, 14 nahi.\n\n**Galti 2: Position check karte waqt diameter se compare karna**\nDoori hamesha **radius** se compare hoti hai. Diameter 12, doori 7: r = 6, to point **bahar** hai, andar nahi.\n\n**Galti 3: Har chord ko diameter samajhna**\nSirf wahi chord diameter hai jo **centre se guzre**. Har diameter chord hai, par har chord diameter nahi.\n\n**Galti 4: Circle aur circular region ko ek samajhna**\nCircle sirf **kinaara (boundary)** hai. Kinaara + andar ka hissa = circular region. Chudi ek circle jaisi hai, roti ek circular region jaisi.\n\n**Galti 5: Circle aur circumference ko ek samajhna**\nCircle ek **shape** hai. Circumference us shape ki **lambai** (ek number) hai.\n\n**Galti 6: Tangent ko do points par kaatne wali line samajhna**\nDo points par kaatne wali line **secant** hai. Tangent sirf **ek point** par chhooti hai.\n\n**Galti 7: Centre ko circle par maan lena**\nCentre circle ke **andar** hota hai. Circle ke saare points centre se r doori par hain, aur centre ki apni doori 0 hai.\n\n**Galti 8: Arc aur chord ko ek samajhna**\nChord **seedha** line segment hai. Arc circle ka **curve wala** tukda hai. Chudi ka toota tukda arc hai, uske dono siron ko jodne wala seedha dhaaga chord hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Circle:** ek plane mein ek fix point (**centre**) se fix doori (**radius**) wale saare points.\n- **Chord:** circle ke do points ko jodne wala segment. **Diameter:** centre se guzarne wali chord, **= 2r**, aur **sabse lambi chord**.\n- Ek circle mein **anginat radius aur diameter** hote hain, sab barabar.\n- **Arc:** circle ka curve wala tukda (detail Topic 2 mein).\n- **Circumference = 2πr = πd.**\n- Circle plane ko **interior, circle, exterior** mein baant deta hai. Circle + interior = **circular region**.\n- **Segment:** chord aur arc ke beech. **Sector:** do radius aur arc ke beech. **Semicircle:** diameter se bana aadha circle.\n- **Secant:** do points par kaatti hai. **Tangent:** ek point par chhooti hai.\n- **Concentric circles:** same centre, alag radius.\n- **Point ki position:** d < r andar, d = r par, d > r bahar. **Radius se compare karo.**",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Circle:** ek plane mein ek fix point (**centre**) se fix doori (**radius**) wale saare points.\n- **Chord:** circle ke do points ko jodne wala segment. **Diameter:** centre se guzarne wali chord, **= 2r**, aur **sabse lambi chord**.\n- Ek circle mein **anginat radius aur diameter** hote hain, sab barabar.\n- **Arc:** circle ka curve wala tukda (detail Topic 2 mein).\n- **Circumference = 2πr = πd.**\n- Circle plane ko **interior, circle, exterior** mein baant deta hai. Circle + interior = **circular region**.\n- **Segment:** chord aur arc ke beech. **Sector:** do radius aur arc ke beech. **Semicircle:** diameter se bana aadha circle.\n- **Secant:** do points par kaatti hai. **Tangent:** ek point par chhooti hai.\n- **Concentric circles:** same centre, alag radius.\n- **Point ki position:** d < r andar, d = r par, d > r bahar. **Radius se compare karo.**"
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. Fill in the blanks:\n   (a) The diameter of a circle is ______ times its radius.\n   (b) The longest chord of a circle is its ______.\n   (c) A point whose distance from the centre equals the radius lies ______ the circle.\n   (d) Circles having the same centre but different radii are called ______ circles.\n   (e) A line that touches a circle at exactly one point is called a ______.\n\n2. The radius of a circle is 4.2 cm. Find its diameter and circumference. (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n3. The circumference of a circle is 154 cm. Find its radius. (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n4. A circle has centre O and radius 6 cm. Points A, B and C are such that OA = 4 cm, OB = 6 cm and OC = 8.5 cm. State the position of each point with respect to the circle.\n\n5. A circle has its centre at the origin and radius 10 units. State whether each point lies inside, on or outside the circle:\n   (a) (6, 8)  (b) (5, 5)  (c) (0, −10)  (d) (11, 0)\n\n6. State whether each statement is true or false. Give a reason.\n   (a) Every chord of a circle is a diameter.\n   (b) A circle has infinitely many radii.\n   (c) A tangent cuts a circle at two points.\n   (d) The centre of a circle lies in its interior.\n   (e) The line segment joining any two points on a circle is a chord.\n\n7. The radius of a circle is 5 cm. Can it have a chord of length 12 cm? Give a reason.\n\n8. A goat is tied to a peg with a rope 14 m long.\n   (a) Find the length of the boundary of the region it can graze. (Take π = 22/7.)\n   (b) Can it reach grass placed 10 m from the peg? What about grass placed 15 m from the peg?\n\n9. The diameter of a cycle wheel is 70 cm. How far does the cycle move in one complete revolution of the wheel? How far in 100 revolutions? (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (a) **2**  (b) **diameter**  (c) **on**  (d) **concentric**  (e) **tangent**\n\n2. Diameter = 2 × 4.2 = **8.4 cm**.\n   Circumference = 2 × (22/7) × 4.2 = (22/7) × 8.4 = 22 × 1.2 = **26.4 cm**.\n\n3. 2 × (22/7) × r = 154, yaani (44/7) × r = 154.\n   r = 154 × 7 ÷ 44 = **24.5 cm**.\n   Jaanch: (44/7) × 24.5 = 44 × 3.5 = 154 ✅\n\n4. OA = 4 < 6, to **A andar** hai.\n   OB = 6 = 6, to **B circle par** hai.\n   OC = 8.5 > 6, to **C bahar** hai.\n\n5. (a) √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 = r, to **circle par**.\n   (b) √(25 + 25) = √50 ≈ 7.07 < 10, to **andar**.\n   (c) Doori 10 = r (y-axis par), to **circle par**.\n   (d) Doori 11 > 10 (x-axis par), to **bahar**.\n\n6. (a) **False** ❌. Sirf centre se guzarne wali chord diameter hai.\n   (b) **True** ✅. Circle par anginat points hain, har ek se ek radius.\n   (c) **False** ❌. Tangent sirf ek point par chhooti hai. Do points par kaatne wali line secant hai.\n   (d) **True** ✅. Centre ki doori 0 hai, jo r se kam hai.\n   (e) **True** ✅. Yahi chord ki definition hai (do alag points lene hain).\n\n7. **Nahi.** Sabse lambi chord diameter hoti hai = 2 × 5 = 10 cm. 12 cm > 10 cm, to aisi chord ho hi nahi sakti.\n\n8. (a) Hadd ki lambai = circumference = 2 × (22/7) × 14 = **88 m**.\n   (b) 10 m < 14 m, to **haan**, pahunch jayegi (andar hai). 15 m > 14 m, to **nahi**, bahar hai.\n\n9. Ek chakkar mein cycle utna chalti hai jitni pahiye ki circumference hai.\n   Circumference = π × d = (22/7) × 70 = **220 cm**.\n   100 chakkar mein = 220 × 100 = 22000 cm = **220 m**.\n\nShabaash! Circle ke saare zaroori shabd ab aapke paas hain. Agar koi shabd bhool jao, to bas Gauri bakri ko yaad karo: khoonta centre hai, rassi radius hai, aur uski gol hadd circle hai.\n\n**Agle topic mein (Topic 2):** Circle ke tukde, yaani arcs, ko degree mein kaise naapte hain? Chhota arc (minor) aur bada arc (major) kya hote hain, aur segment ke \"alternate\" hisse ka kya matlab hai? Ye sab Topic 2 mein dekhenge.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. Fill in the blanks:\n   (a) The diameter of a circle is ______ times its radius.\n   (b) The longest chord of a circle is its ______.\n   (c) A point whose distance from the centre equals the radius lies ______ the circle.\n   (d) Circles having the same centre but different radii are called ______ circles.\n   (e) A line that touches a circle at exactly one point is called a ______.\n\n2. The radius of a circle is 4.2 cm. Find its diameter and circumference. (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n3. The circumference of a circle is 154 cm. Find its radius. (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n4. A circle has centre O and radius 6 cm. Points A, B and C are such that OA = 4 cm, OB = 6 cm and OC = 8.5 cm. State the position of each point with respect to the circle.\n\n5. A circle has its centre at the origin and radius 10 units. State whether each point lies inside, on or outside the circle:\n   (a) (6, 8)  (b) (5, 5)  (c) (0, −10)  (d) (11, 0)\n\n6. State whether each statement is true or false. Give a reason.\n   (a) Every chord of a circle is a diameter.\n   (b) A circle has infinitely many radii.\n   (c) A tangent cuts a circle at two points.\n   (d) The centre of a circle lies in its interior.\n   (e) The line segment joining any two points on a circle is a chord.\n\n7. The radius of a circle is 5 cm. Can it have a chord of length 12 cm? Give a reason.\n\n8. A goat is tied to a peg with a rope 14 m long.\n   (a) Find the length of the boundary of the region it can graze. (Take π = 22/7.)\n   (b) Can it reach grass placed 10 m from the peg? What about grass placed 15 m from the peg?\n\n9. The diameter of a cycle wheel is 70 cm. How far does the cycle move in one complete revolution of the wheel? How far in 100 revolutions? (Take π = 22/7.)\n\n### Answers\n\n1. (a) **2**  (b) **diameter**  (c) **on**  (d) **concentric**  (e) **tangent**\n\n2. Diameter = 2 × 4.2 = **8.4 cm**.\n   Circumference = 2 × (22/7) × 4.2 = (22/7) × 8.4 = 22 × 1.2 = **26.4 cm**.\n\n3. 2 × (22/7) × r = 154, yaani (44/7) × r = 154.\n   r = 154 × 7 ÷ 44 = **24.5 cm**.\n   Jaanch: (44/7) × 24.5 = 44 × 3.5 = 154 ✅\n\n4. OA = 4 < 6, to **A andar** hai.\n   OB = 6 = 6, to **B circle par** hai.\n   OC = 8.5 > 6, to **C bahar** hai.\n\n5. (a) √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 = r, to **circle par**.\n   (b) √(25 + 25) = √50 ≈ 7.07 < 10, to **andar**.\n   (c) Doori 10 = r (y-axis par), to **circle par**.\n   (d) Doori 11 > 10 (x-axis par), to **bahar**.\n\n6. (a) **False** ❌. Sirf centre se guzarne wali chord diameter hai.\n   (b) **True** ✅. Circle par anginat points hain, har ek se ek radius.\n   (c) **False** ❌. Tangent sirf ek point par chhooti hai. Do points par kaatne wali line secant hai.\n   (d) **True** ✅. Centre ki doori 0 hai, jo r se kam hai.\n   (e) **True** ✅. Yahi chord ki definition hai (do alag points lene hain).\n\n7. **Nahi.** Sabse lambi chord diameter hoti hai = 2 × 5 = 10 cm. 12 cm > 10 cm, to aisi chord ho hi nahi sakti.\n\n8. (a) Hadd ki lambai = circumference = 2 × (22/7) × 14 = **88 m**.\n   (b) 10 m < 14 m, to **haan**, pahunch jayegi (andar hai). 15 m > 14 m, to **nahi**, bahar hai.\n\n9. Ek chakkar mein cycle utna chalti hai jitni pahiye ki circumference hai.\n   Circumference = π × d = (22/7) × 70 = **220 cm**.\n   100 chakkar mein = 220 × 100 = 22000 cm = **220 m**.\n\nShabaash! Circle ke saare zaroori shabd ab aapke paas hain. Agar koi shabd bhool jao, to bas Gauri bakri ko yaad karo: khoonta centre hai, rassi radius hai, aur uski gol hadd circle hai.\n\n**Agle topic mein (Topic 2):** Circle ke tukde, yaani arcs, ko degree mein kaise naapte hain? Chhota arc (minor) aur bada arc (major) kya hote hain, aur segment ke \"alternate\" hisse ka kya matlab hai? Ye sab Topic 2 mein dekhenge."
          }
