            "headingHinglish": "Part A: Congruent Circles",
            "body": "Congruence chapter ke Topic 1 mein humne dekha tha ki do figures congruent tab hoti hain jab ek ko doosri par rakhne se wo **bilkul dhak** jaye (superposition). Circles par bhi yahi baat lagti hai.\n\nEk circle ki shakal uske **radius** se hi tay hoti hai. Isliye:\n\n> **Do circles congruent hote hain agar aur sirf agar unke radius barabar hon.**\n\n| Circle 1 | Circle 2 | Congruent? |\n|---|---|---|\n| radius 4 cm | radius 4 cm | Haan |\n| radius 4 cm | diameter 8 cm | Haan (diameter 8 matlab radius 4) |\n| radius 4 cm | radius 5 cm | Nahi |\n\nDhyan do: centre kahan hai, isse farak nahi padta. Ek thali mez par ho aur doosri almaari mein, phir bhi dono congruent hain.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Congruence chapter ke Topic 1 mein humne dekha tha ki do figures congruent tab hoti hain jab ek ko doosri par rakhne se wo **bilkul dhak** jaye (superposition). Circles par bhi yahi baat lagti hai.\n\nEk circle ki shakal uske **radius** se hi tay hoti hai. Isliye:\n\n> **Do circles congruent hote hain agar aur sirf agar unke radius barabar hon.**\n\n| Circle 1 | Circle 2 | Congruent? |\n|---|---|---|\n| radius 4 cm | radius 4 cm | Haan |\n| radius 4 cm | diameter 8 cm | Haan (diameter 8 matlab radius 4) |\n| radius 4 cm | radius 5 cm | Nahi |\n\nDhyan do: centre kahan hai, isse farak nahi padta. Ek thali mez par ho aur doosri almaari mein, phir bhi dono congruent hain."
